# SA2A conformance -- NEGATIVE vector: malformed Turtle.
#
# Three independent syntax faults, so no single lenient recovery path rescues it:
#   1. an unterminated IRI  (`<http://example.org/sa2a/agentA` -- no closing `>`)
#   2. an unclosed string literal
#   3. a statement with no terminating `.`
#
# The expected outcome is a PARSE-TIME refusal, distinct in kind from every
# other vector here (which are semantically well-formed graphs that fail a law).
# graphlaw's wasm boundary returns refusals as a JSON `{"error": "..."}` object
# rather than throwing, so the host MUST check for the "error" key.

@prefix ex: <http://example.org/sa2a/> .

<http://example.org/sa2a/agentA a ex:Agent ;
    ex:label "Agent A ;
    ex:version 1
